## SEVERITY / VERDICT (the grading rule is decided HERE; apply it, do not re-argue it)
*Blocker:* a path beyond the one (in the PR or the fix commit); any byte of `.github/**`, `api/**`, `web/**` or another `infra/**` file; a non-ASCII byte, a person's name, a decision-card id, a `B###` token, a `C-<n>` entry number or a ticket key in a test name, an added line or the message; a skip/sleep/retry/environment gate added to a test; the head moved; a textual conflict; a secret; a CodeQL alert open on the head; a failing test at the head (reader or suite, after the file is re-run alone twice, and the red NOT reproduced at main); an existing assertion loosened, deleted or made conditional (C1/C4 mapping broken); code outside the file-level section changed (C2 AST unequal against `adcd0fd`).
*Major, class SAME:* **(M1)** a valid-YAML layout edit (F1, F2, F4, F6, or your own probe from C3(b) green at BASE) that reads RED at HEAD; an invisible-character plant RED at OLD and GREEN at HEAD (regression); a composition cell of C3(d) green at HEAD; a character `str.strip()` removes, outside trailing LF/CR and the disclosed line-break rulings, that stays green at HEAD at a value edge; a mutant that survives AND that you can show hides an invisible edit on a printable `ci.yml` plant; the new method able to pass while a row did not run (a counter that cannot fail); an existing negative-asserting cell that now passes for a different reason (C4). **(M2) a pin weakened:** any assertion of an existing row changed. **(M3)** the unmutated head reader or suite not measured at all. *Major, class DIFFERENT:* a builder claim contradicted by measurement with a verdict consequence (35 reader tests; names lost 0 added 0; 181 rows; 117 red on the both-strip revert; 267 whole-infra; AST equal; one path +92 -23; F1/F2/F4/F6 green at the fix; 70 of 70 red plants; 11 of 11 mutants killed; 20 of 20 check-runs).
*Minor / Note (never a Major):* the survivors n10-n12 and `rstrip(" \t")` if shown equivalent on the real file; the disclosed sibling strip sites (main lines 57, 257, 349, 357/358, 513, 697, 723, 789, 808 and the one plant at 697); U+0085, U+2028, U+2029, trailing LF/CR and the `ref` after the `@` (rulings, B734-9 and B734-6, outside the commission); N3 docstring wording and N4 (no message pin on the `run: |` + U+00A0 cell), carried by the builder as NARROWING; the 3.9 `test_resource_hygiene` failure reproduced at main; the `mkdtemp` leak; `unsigned` commit; the layout code's limit (a start step that already holds `id`, `timeout-minutes` and `working-directory` would make the method error: not a plausible edit; report whether the real file is that close); the runner's Python and the GitHub parse UNMEASURED; the builder's relative-layout and `index_of` signature deviations if they meet Property L.
*Where the line between Note and Major is unclear:* a thing that makes the method unable to fail, hides a plant, or lets a valid edit fail is at least Major SAME; a thing that only narrows how strong a row is, stays true to the commission and is disclosed, is a Note. Say which rule you applied for every finding. **Round 2 of 2 is THE CAP: do not pad a Note into a NO GO and do not soften a Blocker: quote the plant, the row and the number.**
**VERDICT RULES.** GO needs every check clean and measured, the layout plants F1/F2/F4/F6 red at OLD and green at HEAD, the regression arm clean, survivors 0 (Notes aside), 0 findings above Note, and the CI predicate read with `infra (Bicep validate)` `success` on the CURRENT head (a not-finished or NOT STARTED row caps at GO WITH FINDINGS (conditional) with the condition named). GO WITH FINDINGS = Minor/Note/Condition only. NO GO on any Blocker or Major (under the cap: closed instances ship, the residue becomes ticket text). NOT GATED = the head moved or a guarded path moved on main. A security-shaped finding is a STOP for tier 1.
**VERDICT LINES (one place, binding).** **First line of STATUS (placeholder at Step 0: `GATE VERDICT B817: PENDING`; verdict form, ONE line):** `GATE VERDICT B817: #233 <GO|GO WITH FINDINGS|NO GO|NOT GATED> @ 53d4302 (round 2 of 2, THE CAP, on class "the reader strips Unicode white space as space"; counted history: B805 NO GO round 1 of 2 quoted - delta <PR 1 path 139/2 and fix commit 1 path 92/23 by program y; hunks inside old 829-852 y; AST equal vs adcd0fd with control fired y; hygiene y> - B805-1 <F1 F2 F4 F6: base green, round-1 method red n of 4, head green n of 4; own layout probes green at head n of n (base green); composition cells red n of n; regression (red at round-1 method, green at head): n> - plants <P1-P6 base green n of 6, head red n of 6; sweep 64 of 64 y/n; characters outside the builder's set still green: <list|none>; legit set green n of n> - mutants <builder's 11: n killed; mine n5-n12: n killed, survivors <list>; counter cannot fail y/n> - tests <reader 34 -> 35 on 3.14 and 3.9 (adcd0fd 35); rows 137 -> 181; whole infra 266 -> 267 under python3 -I and the CI form; names lost n added n vs adcd0fd> - CI <infra (Bicep validate) <success|in_progress|NOT STARTED> on the head, check-runs n of n, alerts n, rules read> - merge <rc n; main moved y/n> - gitleaks rc <n>)`. Then the sections: Step 0 (sha256s, slot count), REFUSE counts, PINS (start and verdict), instrument and load, Checks C1-C7 each with the FAIL clock and evidence path, findings `B817-n` each with severity, class SAME or DIFFERENT for a Major with the rule applied, `path:line` at the head, instrument, FAIL met, fix-shape in prose, evidence class MEASURED AT RUNTIME / PROBED / READ ONLY, the plant tables (plant, edit, BASE / OLD / HEAD x 3.14 / 3.9), the names table, the CI table (check, predicate, status), **FOR TUESDAY** (the verdict in plain words; whether the head-pinned squash can go, with the exact command below; what is still required before it can; the Q-question on class if rais